From: backport
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: foresee: add F35UQA512M

The Xiaomi AX3000E carries a FORESEE F35UQA512M, which mainline's spi-nand
table does not know:

  spi-nand spi0.0: unknown raw ID cd6060cd00
  spi-nand spi0.0: probe with driver spi-nand failed with error -95

Stock U-Boot identifies it as:

  Serial NAND device Manufacturer:F35UQA512M
  Device Size:64 MiB, Page size:2048, Spare Size:64, ECC:4-bit

so it is the 512Mbit sibling of the F35SQA001G/002G already listed here --
same geometry, half the eraseblocks (512 x 128KiB = 64MiB). Manufacturer id
0xCD is already SPINAND_MFR_FORESEE.

Without this the flash never probes, which on this board also takes out the
nvmem provider that supplies the ethernet MAC and the ART partition that
ath11k needs for board data and calibration.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/foresee.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/foresee.c
@@ -81,6 +81,16 @@
 		     SPINAND_HAS_QE_BIT,
 		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f35sqa002g_ooblayout,
 				     f35sqa002g_ecc_get_status)),
+	SPINAND_INFO("F35UQA512M",
+		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0x60, 0x60),
+		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 512, 10, 1, 1, 1),
+		     NAND_ECCREQ(1, 512),
+		     SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
+					      &write_cache_variants,
+					      &update_cache_variants),
+		     SPINAND_HAS_QE_BIT,
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&f35sqa002g_ooblayout,
+				     f35sqa002g_ecc_get_status)),
 	SPINAND_INFO("F35SQA001G",
 		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0x71, 0x71),
 		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 1024, 20, 1, 1, 1),
